1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The name "Bjorno" was taken because there was a man in the same small town by the name of Richardt Emil Nonnegaard who was the town criminal. Richardt's (this Richardt) business as a baker and his reputation were t
2 CONC arnished due to his identity constantly being mistaken for this criminal. As a result, he changed his name to "Bjorno," which at the time was only a surname in Norway. Therefore all Danish "Bjornos" are related to Richardt. Howeve
2 CONC r, the family relocated to Norway not long after, where Bjorno is a fairly common surname. 
