2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} More about Hulda at http://mankell.org/hw_descendants.html
2 CONT
2 CONT In the summer of 1890, a year after her father's death, Hulda sailed to Gothenburg (Göteborg) Sweden where she had many relatives including Aunts, Hermina and Augusta. She also traveled to Stockholm, the home of her Uncle, Otto A.
2 CONC  Mankell. (Here is brief summary of a much longer love story, documented by many letters.) When Hulda left on this voyage she was engaged to a businessman (Charles Reese) from Minneapolis; when she returned to the US in August 189
2 CONC 1, still engaged, she fell in love with another man, Hans Melgaard, a Norwegian whom she met on board the steamer ship, "Bothnia". Hans wrote to Hulda in September 1891:
2 CONT
2 CONT     I shall never forget the ocean trip on the "Bothnia"... I enjoyed your company so much, and the time seemed to pass away so fast and pleasantly that I was almost wishing that the voyage would last twice as long as it did. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hulda remained engaged to Reese after her return to the US. Yet, Hans continued his courtship of Hulda. Hulda and Hans married in May, 1893 in New London MN. They moved to Argyle Minnesota where Hans was a banker. He organized the
2 CONC  Farmers and Merchants Bank of Argyle in 1886. This was the first bank in Marshall County. Their home was called "Bothnia". (Charles Reese married in 1894 and lived in Willmar.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans died in 1923 at their home in Minneapolis. Eight years later Hulda passed away. Hulda's granddaughter, Jane Pejsa, writes about Hulda's last years:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Hulda's financial situation had been deteriorating for two years, and along with it her heatlh. In a decline that began soon after the stock market crash of 1929, Hans' banks, his land, and his farms were all in foreclosure. W
2 CONC orse yet, even Hulda's Minneapolis home and her cottage at Maple Lake were in jeopardy. Still, she continued to put up a brave front as the hostess with the mostest. Especially at Christmas, Hulda still included into her "Swedish 
2 CONC Jul" celebration all the lonely and abandoned ones from her large friendship circle. In early December of 1931, Hulda suffered a massive stroke. She lived a number of days after that, but was fully paralyzed on one side. On Christ
2 CONC mas Day, Hulda Mankell Melgaard died at home. Her last words were, "Be sure to have Christmas here and invite those who are alone." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hulda and Hans had 6 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Agnes (1894-1984)
2 CONT     Irene (1896-1990) m. Walter Hauser
2 CONT     Ruth (1898-1994) m. Frederick Sill
2 CONT     Mildred (1901-1996) m. Caradoc Rees
2 CONT     Harold (1903-1986) m. Josepha Knutson
2 CONT     Carmen (1912-1999) m. Leon Holman
2 CONT
2 CONT Letter written by Anne Melgard Holen, Hans sister, regarding his marriage to a Swedish girl, Hulda.
2 CONT
2 CONT Argyle , Minnesota, Dcbr . 5th 1892
2 CONT
2 CONT Dear Parents and Siblings !
2 CONT
2 CONT Now it is not rather than I can remember one year tomorrow since I last wrote to you for thus one year in the night was , since we had the terrible snow storm and fire also who was not so easy to forget. Our building along the ban
2 CONC k is now fully capable again, and so much more massive, and that it is not to compare with eh we had last time _ I have heard several say that Olson & Holen has the finest and largest office building in the North - West. Brother H
2 CONC anses private residence is now also soon in full condition for his Swedish " Flikka " . Wha do they think of him to mingle in with the Swedes then? Were they not a little surprised when they got to hear that he was engaged etc and
2 CONC  with something so strange and unacquainted all of us. ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Yes it does not really concern us Siblings by huh she is or how she is when he thinks about her, but I know many in Argyle that keeps him too good for her. She is not in the least handsome , but hope she is des kinder ! However, I
2 CONC  think that whoever girl whether she was Norwegian or Swedish would be kind to him who is so patiently and good-natured self and forskaffer his wife as an elegant home , and all other matters of great black immediately she enters 
2 CONC . _ She will the finest and costliest home here in Argyle and I do not believe that she will need to tøie his patience difficult much as long as she is with him. For my part I have also liked to see Mary Forr in her place and thin
2 CONC k also that he has been just as well served thereby . Maria is a much prettier Dame and just as kind as also I think she's like the he ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Name:	Hulda E Melgaard and daughter Carmen age 11 Arrival Date:	22 Aug 1924 Birth Date:	3 Aug 1868 Birth Location:	Minnesota Birth Location Other:	st cloud Age:	55 Gender:	Female Port of Departure:	Southampton Port of Arrival:	New
2 CONC  York, New York Ship Name:	Aquitania
2 CONT
