1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Who's Who in America, The Book of Minnesotans. 
2 CONT
2 CONT MELGAARD, Hans L., banker; born in Norway, Nov. 4, 1859; son of Lars H. and Anne Meigaard; common school education. Was bookkeeper at Lillehammer, Norway, until 1882; came to America, 1882, and was bookkeeper First National Bank o
2 CONC f Fargo, N. D.; removed to Argyle, Minn., and founded the Farmers and Merchants Bank of Argyle, 1886. of which he is president. Also president State Bank of Kennedy, State Bank of Karlstad. Scandla State Bank of Stephens, State Ba
2 CONC nk of Middle River, Citizens State Bank of Osto; vice president State Bank of Warren, Farmers State Bank, of Newfolden. State Bank of Bandette, Bank of Viking. Bank of Alvarado. Owns and operates farm near Argyle. Republican. Mayo
2 CONC r of Argyle; delegate to Republican National Convention at Philadelphia, 1900. Lutheran. Mason (32°). Married in Minnesota, 1893. to Miss Hulda Mankell. Address: Argyle, Minn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the publication, “A Self Portrait of Marshall County” there is this reference:
2 CONT
2 CONT Early days of Argyle:  By the mid-1880’s Hans Melgard (note spelling change) had arrived to open a bank on the rear lot leased to J.J. Stone for a granary.  In 1891, a fire broke out during a snowstorm and an entire block of busin
2 CONC esses south of the Melgard bank were gone.  Several years later Hans and Ole Melgard teamed up to build the Farmers and Merchants Bank.  Hans Melgards bank building was later purchased, moved to a new lot, and transformed into a p
2 CONC ost office.  In 1905 a grain elevator and potato warehouse became the property of the Farmers and Merchants Company and was reported to be doing a flourishing business.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 1903 Warren Newspaper lists several real estate transfers from State of Minnesota to Hans Melgaard and Ferdinand Keye.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to family member, Hulda died 8 yrs. after Hans.  His banks, land, farms, etc. had all gone into foreclosure as a result of the 1929 stock market crash. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans at the age of 14 worked in his uncle Erik’s store for three years, while Erik's son Hans Myhre attended the County or District School. (From Myhre's family stories)
2 CONT
2 CONT Letter from sister Anne Melgard Holen to parents and siblings in Norway regarding Hans marrying a Swedish girl! Argyle , Minnesota, Dcbr . 5th 1892
2 CONT
2 CONT Dear Parents and Siblings !
2 CONT
2 CONT Now it is not rather than I can remember one year tomorrow since I last wrote to you for thus one year in the night was , since we had the terrible snow storm and fire also who was not so easy to forget. Our building along the ban
2 CONC k is now fully capable again, and so much more massive, and that it is not to compare with eh we had last time _ I have heard several say that Olson & Holen has the finest and largest office building in the North - West. Brother H
2 CONC anses private residence is now also soon in full condition for his Swedish " Flikka " . Wha do they think of him to mingle in with the Swedes then? Were they not a little surprised when they got to hear that he was engaged etc and
2 CONC  with something so strange and unacquainted all of us. ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Yes it does not really concern us Siblings by huh she is or how she is when he thinks about her, but I know many in Argyle that keeps him too good for her. She is not in the least handsome , but hope she is des kinder ! However, I
2 CONC  think that whoever girl whether she was Norwegian or Swedish would be kind to him who is so patiently and good-natured self and forskaffer his wife as an elegant home , and all other matters of great black immediately she enters 
2 CONC . _ She will the finest and costliest home here in Argyle and I do not believe that she will need to tøie his patience difficult much as long as she is with him. For my part I have also liked to see Mary Forr in her place and thin
2 CONC k also that he has been just as well served thereby . Maria is a much prettier Dame and just as kind as also I think she's like the he ...
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1920 the family had moved to Minneapolis.  According to the census they were living at 2002 Pillsbury Ave. which is at the corner of Franklin and Pillsbury Ave.  South Minneapolis.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Argyle opened its first bank -- the Farmer's and Merchant's Bank -- in 1886. In the bank's advertisement in the Banner, it asserted that it was the oldest bank in Marshall County. Hans L. Melgaard was president of the bank, and Ol
2 CONC e Melgaard was cashier.
