1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ole L. Melgaard:
2 CONT
2 CONT He left Norway in 1876 with an uncle to America, landing in Philadelphia during the Exposition and then continued on to Black River Falls.  He finished his education and learned the English language while working on his uncle’s fa
2 CONC rm.  He then worked in La Crosse, WI. married Julia, and moved to Argyle.  In 1889 he became cashier of the Farmers State Bank of which his oldest brother was President. From Findagrave Woodlawn cemetery Argyle Marshall Co. MN Bir
2 CONC th: 	Nov., 1861, Norway Death: 	Feb. 27, 1941 Marshall County Minnesota, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Farm Workers Burial
2 CONT  	Township Alma Twp	City Argyle	Active/Inactive Inactive Street Address
