2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Kennedy Cemetery  Kennedy Kittson County Minnesota, USA 1910 census living in Tegner, Kittson County, with four children and sister-in-law Carrie.  Wife had died a few days after birth of 4th child Petra Louise.  He later 
2 CONC married Carrie and had one mor child, Trygve.  1920 census wife Cary who immigrated in 1892.  5 children listed. Louis Philip Melgaard, Oscar Henry Melgaard, Anna Sophia Melgaard, Petra Louise Melgaard, Norman Trygve Melgaard  He 
2 CONC is a banker, State Bank. 1930 census Living on Fourth street Kennedy.  Immigrated in 1892.  Occupation Manager real estate and insurance.  He and spouse our 61 yrs old.  Son Norman 18 a salesman hardware store. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1894 working for E. E. (Edward E.) Seielstad and Hougen Wholesate Grocers in LaCrosse, WI. source..letter written by him to family back in Norway. This is probably where he first settled.  And a letter from there in 1897.  Then 19
2 CONC 08 from Bank of Kennedy. There are two generations of E. E. Seielstad who had the business.  See Edvard Segelstad who's father was Engebret, brother of Eli Gudbrandsd Segelstad. 5 Story building on Front Street, La Crosse. Bldg.No
2 CONC  bldg. left. 1912 State Bank of Kennedy incorporated with brother H. L. Melgard president and Lauritz cashier.  1912 part of a group oranganizing a farm elevator company in Kennedy.  1918 listed as President Northcote State Bank. 
2 CONC  He and his brother who emigrated from Norway were all involved in the banking business mainly in NW Minn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Warren Sheaf...Lauritz and brother Torger traveled to Norway May 1900 and then possibly on to the Paris Exhibition. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Norwegian American Evangelical Church records have his baptism recorded in 1910 living in Kennedy MN.  
