1 NOTE {geni:about_me} An excerpt from a writeup by Torger's son, Thomas Lee, on his retirement years:
2 CONT
2 CONT Torger L. Melgaard came to Thief River Falls from Larimore, North Dakota in 1903 to help establish a bank.  The Citizens State Bank opened to the public on July 8, 1903 as a private bank with D. B. Bakke as President and T. L. Mel
2 CONC gaard, Cashier.  On Sept 17, 1903 through the efforts of Mr. Melgaard, the bank was reorganized and incorporated with a capital of $20000.  Later on, the bank moved to the corner of LaBree and Third Street.  This was considered th
2 CONC e finest structure in the city, if not in the midwest.  The Melgaard family resided at 520 East First Street.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1901 living in Black River Falls,Wi. where they were recently married.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 1920 census living in Pennington, MN.  1930 census Alameda Ca. both times with spouse Rena E. 
2 CONT
