1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Early member of Gudgrandslaget America.
2 CONT
2 CONT Became a widow in 1911 and does not look like he remarried.  A nephew Louis P. Melgard was living with him in 1940.  He traveled back to Norway at least two times, 1939 SS Bergensfjord Oslo to NY and 1956 SS Stavangerfjord Oslo to
2 CONC  NY with daughter Alice White Melgard.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Findagrave #22571780 Moscow Cemetery Moscow Latah County Idaho, USA Plot: Old Section Block 4
2 CONT
2 CONT  Alex Prus and Laura Kross JAMM225 Mapping Main Street: Second and Third Streets
2 CONT
2 CONT The Spokane and Eastern Bank of Spokane opened a branch in Spicer Block on the corner of Second Street and Main in 1900. In 1906 the Spokane and Eastern Bank of Spokane was purchased by Hawkin and Andrew Melgard (brothers) and was
2 CONC  called The Moscow Branch of the Spokane and Eastern.The Moscow Branch of the Spokane and Eastern was officially called The First Trust and Savings Bank in 1914. 1946 sold controlling interest in bank and retired as president and 
2 CONC remained chairman of the board. 
2 CONT
2 CONT First Trust & Savings Bank building, built in 1921 by Hawkin Melgard and razed in 1963. Moscow,  Idaho. 
2 CONT
2 CONT MELGARD, Hawkin, 221-225 Main St.; res. 317 North Hayes St., Moscow, Idaho. Banker; b. Hundorp, Norway, Jan. 17, 1880; s. of Lars H. and Anne 0. Melgard: ed. public high schools, Norway; m. Kennewick. Wash.. July 15, 1006, Winnie 
2 CONC A. Kennedy (d.): children; Alice Gladys, Helen Winifred, Thelma Solvel*. Arrived In 0. 8. 1898; clerk Bank of Brsklne, Minn., l«0fl 1901: assistant cashier Seundla State Bunk of Stephen. Minn.. 1901-1802; rem oved to Goldendalo, W
2 CONC ash., 1002: cashier and pre*. State Bank of Goldendale 1902-00; sec and mgr. First Trust Co., Moscow. Idaho, now First Trust and Saving! Bank, of which he Is pres. Now Mayor of city of Moscow, and pres. Moscow Board of Education ,
2 CONC  treas. Moscow Chamber of Commerce. Member County Council of Defense, and every Liberty I>nan Committee. Member National Geographic Society, National Re publican League. Mason, Shrtuer. Elk, Odd Fellow. Modern Woodmen of America. 
2 CONC Club: Moscow Shrine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Name:	Hakon L Melgaard Arrival Date:	12 May 1898 Birth Date:	abt 1880 Age:	18 Gender:	Male Ethnicity/ Nationality:	Norwegian Port of Departure:	Liverpool, England Port of Arrival:	New York, New York Ship Name:	Majestic Final desti
2 CONC nation Argyle MN to join his brother H. Melgard
