1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John David Rees
2 CONT
2 CONT March 16, 1932 – July 18, 2021
2 CONT
2 CONT Our incredible uncle and wonderful friend John David Rees crossed over at the ripe young age of 89.
2 CONT
2 CONT John was truly a renaissance man, who spent much of his life in the style of Indiana Jones. His passion for botany led to his searching the jungles and deserts of Central America for rare and undiscovered Cycads and Palms.
2 CONT
2 CONT This dedication led to a long career in education obtaining his MA and PHD in Geography at UCLA, followed by a long tenure at Cal State Los Angeles in the Geography Department.
2 CONT
2 CONT His service in the US Army ROTC program fueled his fervent interests in military history, militaria and cavalry arms, as well as international travel and politics.
2 CONT
2 CONT John never sat still and remained deeply connected to his numerous gardens and hobbies till his passing. Well into his 80's he embraced learning, taking classes in everything from art to automobile repair and restoration. His comm
2 CONC itment to his friends and love of life will be dearly missed by all who he touched.
2 CONT
2 CONT John is survived by his nephews, James Rees and Evan Rees, his long-time partner Clarissa Dong, and multiple cousins throughout the US
