1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://mankell.org/borgen.html   
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/40565528/bor
2 CONT
2 CONT Margit Syvertsdatter was born in Norway, probably in Buskerud County, on March 2, 1812. Aside from the fact that her father was obviously named Syvert, her parents are unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometime around 1838, she married Swen Gunderson Borgen, probably in Numedal, Buskerud. They had at least three children there, one of them born in Numedal. Margit and Swen, with their children, came to America around 1855 or so. 
2 CONC They spent some time in Rock County, Wisconsin, because their daughter Birgitte was married there in 1859. They wound up in the East Norway Lake area of Kaddiyohi County, Minnesota, where they spent the rest of their lives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margit died in Kandiyohi County on July 26, 1891 and is buried in the East Norway Lake Lutheran Church Cemetery in Pennock. (research by Ken)
