1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/75267794/erik-hansen-roms%C3%A5s
2 CONT
2 CONT ?? today...FRAMIGARD ROMSÅS ANS is a ranching company based out of Brekkomsvegen 519, FÅVANG, 519 Fv378 Ringebu, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Industries Ranching Headquarters FÅVANG, Ringebu Locations Brekkomsvegen 519
2 CONT
2 CONT FÅVANG, Ringebu 2634, NO
2 CONT
2 CONT Fv383 nearest main road 
2 CONT
2 CONT Norske Gaardnavne (Norwegian farm Names) Oluf Rygh.	 106. 107. Myre øvre og nedre. Udt. mý2re. -- Myre 1520. Miøre 1578. Myrre 1594. Mhyrre 1604.1/1. Myre (2 Gaarde) 1668. (2 Gaarde) 1723.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Mýrar, Flt. af mýrr f., Myr.Erik's father Hans Larsen Romsas  bought Ovre (upper) Myhre farm in 1840.  He drowned in the Laugen River while trying to cross it on ice at the age of 36.  He left his widow  Marit with 5 children inc
2 CONC luding Erik Hansen Myhre. Marit remarried and had six more children.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik operated a store at Tromsnes near Fåvang where son Hans was born.  In 1891 Erik and Eli Gulbransdatter  moved to her family's farm,  Segelstad farm and purchased the Segelstad Nedre (Nigard) farm from Johannes Gulbrandsons.  
2 CONC Nedre or Nigard means lower. (the river is called Tromsa. The town of Tromsnes was changed to Fåvang 1921, the same for Myre railway station.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Letter from Hans Melgard living in Ringebo to his parents..."Uncle is now in the process of buying the farm from Johannes Seielstad and Ole Rørvig will acquire Odnes if they can agree on the terms, which I'm confident they will."
2 CONT Trader Erik H. Myhre bought the plot of land Odnes for 40 spd from Rørvik in 1869. Here he had operated as a free trader from before 1865.
2 CONT Picture is Odnes in 1893.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He changed his name from Myhre to Segelstad (also seen as Seielstad on various documents). All of his children except Hans took the Segelstad name.  Hans had already emigrated to the US and used the Myhre name. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Norges matrikel 1904 for Kristians amt (Oppland) del
2 CONT  Mellem Gudbrandsdalen sorenskriveri Nordre Fron, Søndre Fron, Ringebu og Øier herreder Matrikulerede eiendomme og deres skyld den 1 januar 1904  Segelstad nedre Segelstad nedre Erik ... H. Myhre.. ... Nordjordet ........ Nils Ive
2 CONC rsen Seielstad Palsveen. .....,... E. Bstensen Palsvee
2 CONT
2 CONT Norske Gaardnavne (Norwegian farm names) Oluf Rygh 104. 105. Segalstad øvre og nedre. Udt. se2ggalsta. -- a Sighualstaudum DN. III 166, 1336 Sewalstadh DN. II 712, 1491 Seualdstad 1520. Sewolstadt 1557. Segelstadt 1578. Seigelstad
2 CONC  1594. Seuolldstad OC. Sygelstad 1604.1/1, 1/1. Seigelstad med Dyrholmen (2 Gaarde) 1668. Seigelstad (2 Gaarde) 1723.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigvaldsstaðir eller Sigvaldastaðir, se S. Fron GN. 26.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography in Seielstad My Heritage family profile.. Census of 1865: Erik lived as his own household on the  Rørviknesset, , where there was another family.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Census of 1875: Erik, Eli and the children Hans, Marit, Guldbrand, and Marie lived on Odnæs together with maidens, bakers and garrdskar. 2 cows, 1 pig and 1 th of barley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Census 1900: Erik, Eli and the children Marit and Gudbrand lived at "Segelstad Nedre
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo showing location of farms is from "Bygdu Var Lokalhistorie for Ringebu" by Einar Hovdaugen.  Page 22-23.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Frihandler, eget hushold..frihandler roughly someone who sell goods with out regulation..probably like a door-to door saleman) 1865
2 CONT   Rørviknesset, Fåvang 	Landhandler,Selveier og Gaardbr. 1875
2 CONT   Odnes, Fåvang
2 CONT
2 CONT Kjøper gården av svogeren Johannes G. Segelstad 1891
2 CONT   Segelstad Nigard, Fåvang
2 CONT
2 CONT The people in this old picture are unknown. But one sees the seal and barn to Nedre Segelstad. In the background you see a Veslefjellet. (And "scared" between the Veslefjellet and the Segelstadseterkampen). A bit strange to see ho
2 CONC w the prospect up is without trees. 1910 Census Residence	1910
