2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/97777865/mathea-arnesdatter-myhre
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Hanson Myhre, along with his wife Mathea, emigrated in 1867 coming to Lanesboro, Minnesota, where they settled on a farm and for fifteen years he resided there attempting to raise his family despite year after year of grassh
2 CONC opper infestations that stripped the fields of his harvest.  In 1876 his wife died in childbirth and she and the child were buried at Lanesboro by the graves of three other infants who had died in the previous years. Reference is 
2 CONC to Lanesboro which is very close to the Root Prairie Church of Fountain, Minnesota, which they belonged to.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She and her child are buried at Root Prairie Cemetery, Fountain, Fillmore County, Minnesota.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried with her mother Marthea Myhre who died in childbirth. A shared stone says "wife of Jacob Myhre and her little daughter 17 days old.
