1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/75267962/eli-gudbrandsdtr-segelstad
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:	Nov 12 1832 Marriage:	Marriage to: Erik Hansen Romsås Myhre Apr 13 1869
2 CONT   Ringebu Kirke Christening:	2 DEC
2 CONT   Ringebu Kirke Death:	Feb 13 1919
2 CONT
2 CONT Eli's family is connected to the Segelstad farms beginning in the late 1700's. Eli was born on Øvre Segelstad.  Her husband Erik purchased Nedre/Nigard Segelstad where they lived for a number of years and were living there at the 
2 CONC time of her death.  After Erik's death the farm went to a son Gulbrand and then after his death to a daugther Marie.  The eldest son Hans had emigrated to America but it was understood that if he returned to Norway he could claim 
2 CONC his rightful inheritance.   Upon Marie's death there were no more siblings  left nor children of these sibling (Gulbrand had three children but was not married and did not live with them and their mother) s. The farm was sold and 
2 CONC proceeds and contents were inherited by Han's daughter Eva and son Erik.  A number of items were donated to the Maighaugen Museum in Lillehammer. The current owners are descendants of Eli's brother who had sold the farm to Erik an
2 CONC d Eli. See brother  Østen Gudbrandsen Segelstad.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a famous story of a Brendon Segelstad who killed a Colonel George Sinclair (Scottish mercenary) at the Battle of Kringen in 1612.  Brendon was living at Øvre Segelstad at the time but I do not believe he and Eli's family 
2 CONC are related.  They did not acquire the farms until the late 1700's and it is said that Brendon's family no longer have any living ancestor. Berdon son Jørgen's 2nd wife Karen Haldorsdtr. Romsås is a brother to Peder Haldorsen Roms
2 CONC ås, Sue's 9th ggrandfather.  Colonel George Sinclair is the 1st cousin 10 times removed from Steve Erickson through his 2nd great grandmother Mary Jane St. Clair.  He is also very distantly related to another of Sue's Norwegian an
2 CONC cestors through the Skanke line. 
2 CONT
2 CONT So Sue's 2nd Great Grandmother Eli and Steve's 2nd great Grandmother Mary Jane have this connection.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 1910 census Eli Segelstad Gender:	Female Birth:	Nov 12 1832
2 CONT   Ringebu, Oppland, Norway Residence:	1910
2 CONT   Segelstad Nedre (Gaard), Ringebu, Oppland, Norway Residential Status:	Present Habitant Age:	77 Marital status:	Married Husband:	Erik Segelstad Children:	Marit Segelstad Marie Segelstad Gudbrand Segelstad Census Source ID:	36433	
2 CONC County Number:	05 Municipality Number:	0520	Census District:	Mitstrand Census District Number:	006	Residence Number:	0023 Farm number:	105	Subfarm Number:	1 Person Number:	002	Household Number:	01 See household members Household R
2 CONC elation to head	Name	Birth Head	Erik Segelstad	Dec 8 1831 Housewife	Eli Segelstad	Nov 12 1832 Daughter	Marit Segelstad	Jan 31 1871 Daughter	Marie Segelstad	Sep 17 1874 Son	Gudbrand Segelstad	Oct 30 1872 Servant	Anette Bystadhaugen
2 CONC 	Oct 30 1894 Servant	Ole Kristianstuen	Oct 10 1887
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo of three farms before one was moved.   Segelstadgardene Dette bildet er tatt da alle tre Segelstadgardene lå i ei klynge; Nedistuen Segelstad, Nedre Segelstad og bak skimter en husa på Øvre Segelstad. For noen tiår siden fly
2 CONC tta Øvre Segelstad husa sine litt bort fra de to andre gardene. Segelstadgardene This picture was taken when all three Sail Stages were in a cluster; Nedistuen Segelstad, Nedre Segelstad and rear glimpse a house on Upper Segelstad
2 CONC . A few decades ago, Upper Segelstad moved their houses away from the other two curtains
2 CONT
2 CONT Regarding transporting for a funeral to the Ringebu church.."Think they used a boat over the laugen before the bridge came. There went an old way up to the liagardan that passed by / through the bystad and the segelstadgardene. Th
2 CONC ere were two roads that they could use. One went after the geilen with the field to segelstad lower on one side and nistuen on others. This one came right beyond the gardstunet to the bystad. The other one went further up, and mor
2 CONC e straight down the field to the lower side of the road. There is still a gate called kjørkjeleet, and it is said that it is called it since they used that road when they were going to the church in the winter. There was also a ro
2 CONC ad that went about the road trip."
