1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Florence Gustaveson was the third of three children born to Andrew Gustave and Anna Svardal Gustaveson. Her parents were farming by the bridge along the Black River in Greenwood, Wisconsin when her father died in 1
2 CONC 904 of TB. Florence's mother married Stephen Cunningham, the hired hand on the farm.  In 1908 they moved to a farm on a beautiful lot 6 miles east of Moscow, Idaho.  Three sons were born to her mother and step-father. Florence was
2 CONC  a beautiful woman, inside and out. She was brilliant and hard working. While working at a local bank, she fell in love with one of the owners and married him - Walter Melgard. After her marriage, life had many new luxuries she ha
2 CONC d never known.. She never forgot the hard work both she and her parents had to perform to survive.  Florence and Walter had one daughter who died as an infant and a son Robert who married Catherine Curtis and had three children.  
2 CONC Walter died 14 years before Florence, who spend much of her widowed years volunteering in programs that helped the needy, always commenting that her own life was not so different the first 30 years, as those she was helping. Flore
2 CONC nce was a beloved person to all who knew her.
2 CONT
2 CONT 207 North Hayes, Moscow, East Moscow, Latah, Idaho, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:	Andrew Gustave Gustaveson Annie Helene Svardal Husband:	Walter Robert Melgard Daughter:	Helen Jean Melgard Siblings:	Palmer Gustaveson Peter Gustaveson Joseph Cunningham Carl C Cunningham Francis Arner Cunningham Eva Cunn
2 CONC ingham Alma Svardal Sanvick
2 CONT
2 CONT Very active in Job's Daughters honored as Supreme Guardian.
