1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Andrew “Bob” Melgard September 26, 1934 - June 5, 2005 Robert Andrew “Bob” Melgard, 70, passed away on Sunday,  June 5, 2005 in Spokane, WA.  Funeral services will be held at 3:00 pm, Friday,  June 10, 2005 
2 CONC at the Jesuit House, 1106 N. Astor, Spokane, with Fr. Ken Krall  officiating. The family requests those attending wear bright colors in honor of  Bob.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bob was born on September 26,  1934 in Moscow, Idaho to Walter and Florence Melgard.  He grew up and  attended schools in Moscow graduating from Moscow High School. He attended the  University of Idaho and became a member of Phi G
2 CONC amma Delta. He graduated from  the University in 1957 with a Bachelor of Science degree in Business.
2 CONT
2 CONT While attending the U of I, Bob met Catherine Curtis in a  photography class. They were married on July 12, 1958 in Sandpoint, Idaho. They  lived in Moscow where Bob opened a women’s clothing store called Roban’s; named  after his
2 CONC  two sons Andrew and Robert. In 1974 Bob moved his family to Spokane,  Washington where they have lived for past 30 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bob had a passion for life, family and people. He believed  all aspects of life should focus around his family. He adored his wife Catherine  of 47 years and believed he was the luckiest man alive to share his life with  her. He w
2 CONC as actively involved in his three children and grandchildren’s lives  and never missed an opportunity to entertain, take trips with his family and go  to the cabin in Sandpoint. Bob had a gift for understanding people. He liked  n
2 CONC othing more than to meet new people and learn their story. He always was on the  phone or writing letters to family, friends and new people he had met to tell  them how much they had touched his life. Bob will always be remembered
2 CONC  for his  talent in photography. There was rarely a time when he didn’t have a camera in  his hands taking pictures of people and events. He enjoyed giving his  photographs to those he had captured on film.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bob is survived by his  family, wife Catherine Melgard of Spokane, children and grandchildren: Andy and  Tyler Melgard of Spokane, Bob, Emily and Grace Melgard of Boise, Idaho and  Kirsten, David and Jack Parker of Boise, Idaho.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death  by his parents, Walter and Florence, and sister Rose Melgard of Moscow, Idaho.
