1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Richard D. Melgard
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Warren, Minnesota on Jul. 9, 1930 Departed on Feb. 19, 2010 and resided in Janesville, WI.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation:	Friday, Feb. 26, 2010 10:00 am - 12 pm Service:	Friday, Feb. 26, 2010 12 pm Cemetery:	Oak Hill Cemetery
2 CONT
2 CONT JANESVILLE--- Richard D. Melgard, age 79, of Janesville, passed away on Friday, Feb. 19, 2010, at Mercy Hospital. He was born in Warren, MN, on July 9, 1930, the son of Homer Quentin “H.Q.” and Alice (Forslund) Melgard. Richard se
2 CONC rved in the US Army tank corps during the Korean War. He moved to Janesville in 1954, and worked for Fisher Body/ General Motors for 18 years before medically retiring in 1972. Richard married Janet M. Schaefer on Dec. 12, 1954, i
2 CONC n Janesville. His interests included John Deere and True Value collectables, playing cards, reading newspapers and automobile magazines. He also enjoyed watching sports on television. Being unable to get out and about, Richard alw
2 CONC ays looked forward to and enjoyed visits from family and friends. He is survived by his wife, Janet; daughter, Linda (Dan) Zumstein; and grandson, Jason Collins all of Janesville; a brother, Calvin (Betty) Melgard of Warren, MN; s
2 CONC pecial friends, Jill and Mike Rowe of Janesville; nieces, nephews, other relatives and friends. He was preceded in death by his parents and 2 brothers, Homer and Robert Melgard. Funeral services will be held at 12:00 p.m. on Frida
2 CONC y, Feb. 26, 2010, at ST. PETER’S LUTHERAN CHURCH with Rev. Bruce Gray officiating. Burial will follow in Oak Hill Cemetery. Visitation will take place on Friday from 10:00 a.m. until the hour of service at ST. PETER’S. The family 
2 CONC is being assisted by SCHNEIDER APFEL SCHNEIDER & SCHNEIDER FUNERAL HOME.  The family would like to extend a special thank you to the team effort of Home Health United, Evansville Manor, Visiting Angels, the Sisters and staff of St
2 CONC . Elizabeth Nursing Home, Mercy Hospital and Dr. Lilley for her wonderful care. His positive and joking attitude will be remembered by all.
