1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Charlotta Hedvig got married after 1748 to Wilhelm Julius Ledebur. Wilhelm Julius was a son to customs scribe Hans Ledebur and Elisabeth Sweder, born in Greifwald in the 1st of November 1701. Wilhelm Julius became
2 CONC  firs t a student in Greifwald, after that ordinate to Uppåkra in 7 September 1727, then 2nd assistant vicar in Malmö 1729 and finally vicar in Södra Villie 1739. He got married to Maria Munthe in 1730 in the city o f Lund. Maria 
2 CONC died in 1733. Wilhelm Julius got married again to Anna Christina Wrangel in 1734 in Hyby. Amma Christina was born 1714 and died in 1748. Wilhelm got married a third time to Charlotta Hedvig Bulich. Wilhelm Julius' son, born 1741, 
2 CONC was adopted into trading in the city of Lund in 1772. He was beneficiary to his stepmother, Charlotta Hedvig, and go t from her the property Böttraryd, 1/2 mantal (assessment unit of land), 'frälse' (exemption from land dues to th
2 CONC e Crown ) in Ydre härad, in the region of Östergötland. In 1820 he donated 2000 'riksdaler banco' to the University of Lund a s a scholarship fund in favour for students born in the cities Malmö or Lund. 
