1 OCCU Pharmacist and druggist and the first of a line of doctors and pharmacists who owned the Raeapteek in Reval (Tallinn), Estonia; lord of Haabneeme and Wannamois, close to Tallinn (Reval).
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pharmaciens_Burchard
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes Burchart I (1546-1616), born János Both Bélaváry de Szikava (Hungarian: Szikavai és Bélaváry Both János), was a Baltic German pharmacist and druggist and the first of a line of doctors and pharmacists who owned the Raeapt
2 CONC eek in Tallinn, Estonia, from 1582 to 1911. He was also lord of Haabneeme and Wannamois, close to Tallinn (Reval).<br/>
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Burchart
2 CONT
