1 CONT 1- Data extracted October 1993.
0 @N6000000001365373837@ NOTE Had a farm named Myhre and took Myhre as a family name.  Drowned in Gudransdallaagen. From South Romsaas and bought Upper Myhre. From Llyod George Melgaard.."Bought Ovre Myre from Osten Olsen Myre for 1200 Specic dollars. He was m
1 CONC arried to Marit Eriksdatter Romsaas. He drowned in the Laugen River while trying to cross it on the ice in 1844 at the age of 36 and left his widow with the following children: Lars Hansen Myre who married Ane Melgaard of Hundorp,
1 CONC  Erik Hansen Myhre who married Eli Seielstad, Peder Hansen Myre, Marit Hansdatter Myre who married Kristian Gundersen Myre and bought the Norgard Bjorge, Jakob Hansen Myre who married Mathea Arnesdatter Berg and was the grandfathe
1 CONC r of the Rorvig family. 
0 @N6000000001365373847@ NOTE From Llyod George Melgaard.."Marit Eriksdatter remarried in 1845 with Ole Olsen Myre, son of Ole Ostenses Myre and grandson of Osten Olsen Myre, the previous owner. They had six children, Ole Osen Myre who married Ronnau Engebrets
1 CONC datter Godl(?), Marit Olsdatter Myre who married Jakob Lundemo, Eli Olsdatter Myre, Hans Olsen Myre who married Oline Strande, Osten Olsen Myre who married Vangen, Mari Olsdatter Myre sho married Hans andersen Bystad. 
0 @N6000000001365387024@ NOTE Married Christen Gundersen Myhre.  Bought north Bjørge farm in Ringebu.  Their son Ole ran the farm for many years. He has no descendants. 
0 @N6000000001365387007@ NOTE Hans Uncle, Jacob Hanson Myhre, along with his wife Mathea emigrated in 1867 coming to Lanesboro, Minnesota, where they settled on a farm and for fifteen years he resided there attempting to raise his family despite year after yea
1 CONC r of grasshopeer infestations that stripped his fields of his harvest.  In 1876 his wife died in childbirth and she and the child were buried at Lanesboro by the graves of three other infants who had died in the previous years.  S
1 CONC ix years later in 1882, Jacob decided to try his luck in the dakota territory so with his nin-year-old twin sons and his seven-year old daughter, he started off in a covered wagon with his household goods, twenty head of his cattl
1 CONC e, etc. on that long trip that took him twenty days.  On the way, they stopped for a drink of water at a log cabin on the Cheyenne River and there found that dreaded discease, diphtheria.  The twin sons died of it and were buried 
1 CONC along the river.  He continued on with his daughter Janna to an area north of what became Binford in what was then Dakota Territory.  He dug out the side of a hill a rough and primitive home for them and they lived in it for many 
1 CONC years until he could construct a home.  Jana marriec in 1896 to Mathias Rorvig and the farm became known as the Rorvig farm.  On June 13, 1982 the Rorvig family celebrated the 100th Anniversary of the farm. 
1 CONT Take from Utvadringa til Amerika fra Ringebu, by Einar Hovdhaugen. 
0 @N6000000001365373817@ NOTE Erik and Eli Gulbransdatter  moved to her family's farm,  Segelstad farm and purchased the Segelstad Nedre (Nigard) farm in 1891 from Johannes Gulbrandsons.  Nedre or Nigard means lower.  He changed his name from Myhre to Segelsta
1 CONC d (also seen as Seielstad on various documents). He had operated a store at Tromsnes near Favang where son Hans was born. 
1 CONT Myre name is derived from myr (peat swamp) and indicates moist ground. It was first mentioned in 1520 and it was called a "full farm" for tax purposes in 1604. In 1668 it had been divided into two farms..Ovre and Nedre (upper and 
1 CONC lower) and in the tax reports of 1725, the tax on one farm was 9 skins 9that of a calf, goat or sheep) and 6 skins for the other.  In 1801, Ovre Myre had 4 husmen and Nedre Myhre had 1. And in the records of 1658, Ovre Myre had 1 
1 CONC gelding horse, 1 mare, 8 cows, 2 goats and 4 sheep while Nedre Myre had 3 mares, 8 cows, 3 goats, and 4 sheep.  The crops in those days were barley, oats, and potatoes. 
1 CONT Teh farm was dividied into Ovre Myre and Ovre Sor Myre. in 1897. In 1901 Gina O Onshus bought Ovre Myhre fro  Kr. 8,000 and fora from Ole Olsen Myre. In 1906 Marit Olsdatter Myre who married Jakob Lundemo excercised her rights as 
1 CONC the seniour daughter and bought Ovre Myre back for Kr. 12,350. Jakob Lundemo drowned in 1911 in the laugen River and Marit died a few years later. 1918 Kristian Smerud bought the farm at an auction sale following the death of the 
1 CONC owner for Kr. 24,100. He was married to Aslaug Engebretsendatter Myrmoen. 1951 Adners Kristiansen Ellingsbord received the farm from his fater for Kr. 16,500. But to return to our family connection again, Hans Anderson Bystad boug
1 CONC ht Ovre Sor Myre from the children of Ole Olsen Myre and his wife Marit Eriksdatter Myre. He was married to their daughter, Olsdatter Myre.  1927 Son Andor Hansen Myre and his sister, Marit, bought this farm from their mother for 
1 CONC Kr. 6,700 and fora. Andor's son, Oluf, now farms this farm. 
