1 CONT in the center portion of Sweden which comprises the counties of Kalmar,
1 CONT Jonkoping, and Kronoberg. The use of this name does not point to a parish or
1 CONT county and the first place name is generaly a farm or village within the
1 CONT parish.
1 CONT 2- Data extracted October 1993.
1 CONT !SOURCES:
1 CONT 1- The records of A R Anderson, Syracuse, Utah, the Ole Anderson Family
1 CONT geneaogist.
1 CONT 2- The records of Owen B Anderson, brother, from whose records this data was
1 CONT extracted. A recource not says that this FGR came from FGR 39, Swedish, in the
1 CONT LDS Family History Library.
1 CONT 4- 6 May 1994: Temple|Ready file report.
1 CONT
1 CONT !NOTES:
1 CONT 1- I have found out that the name SMALAND is the name of a province
1 CONT in the center portion of Sweden which comprises the counties of Kalmar,
1 CONT Jonkoping, and Kronoberg. The use of this name does not point to a parish or
1 CONT county and the first place name is generaly a farm or village within the
1 CONT parish.
1 CONT 2- Data extracted October 1993.
0 @N6000000006127509640@ NOTE Överste Gustaf Uggla, som blev inskriven på riddarhuset i Finland år 1818 under nr 4 bland adelsmän, fick 1789 sonen Claes Gustaf. 
0 @N6000000006127509646@ NOTE Efter avsked ur armén som kapten 1834 blev Claes Gustaf kammarherre. Claes Gustafs fick tre söner och dog 1843. Läs vidare i Sveriges Adelskalender. 
0 @N6000000001365373859@ NOTE 1st wife married in 1791, Anne Pedersd. Rørvik.  Bought frammigard Romsås in 1803. 
0 @N6000000001365387775@ NOTE Note from Llyod George Melgaard state it is Erik Knutsen Romsaas (1788-1874) marred Marit Pedersdatter Romsaas b. 1790.
0 @N6000000001365402160@ NOTE Peder went to the USA in 1907 and never came back.  He worked at the Rorvig farm at Ginform, met a woman there and left for Canada.  (source is Jon Ødegård)
0 @N6000000001365390929@ NOTE Farmed the Segelstad farm until his death in 1942. Gudbrand became the father of three children but was not married.  One son Erik Seielstad, age 70 in 1998 was at that time living close to the Segelstad farm.  
0 @N6000000001365373261@ NOTE Hans was born at Tromsnes near Faavang and attended the County or District School. He emigrated to America May 18, 1888 at the age of 19.  He is listed in a book "Utvandringa til Amerika" by Einar Hovhaugen. He traveled on the "An
1 CONC gelo" from Christiania (Oslo) to Hull, England, and eventually came to Black River Falls, WI.  Based on the most common "package ticket", Hans probably traveled by train from Hull to Liverpool or Glasgow, the departure ports of th
1 CONC e Allan Line and then on to Canada or the USA.  Many emigrants who settled in the Midwest came through Quebec rather than New York City. 
1 CONT
1 CONT "Most of the emigrants entering Hull travelled via the Paragon Railway Station and from there travelled to Liverpool via Leeds, Huddersfield and Stalybridge (just outside Manchester). The train tickets were part of a package that 
1 CONC included the steamship ticket to Hull, a train ticket to Liverpool and then the steamship ticket to their final destination - mainly America. Sometimes so many emigrants arrived at one time that there would be up to 17 carriages b
1 CONC eing pulled by one steam engine. All the baggage was stored in the rear 4 carriages, with the passengers filling the carriages nearer the front of the train. The trains took precedence over all other train services because of thei
1 CONC r length and usually left Hull on a Monday morning around 11.00 a.m., arriving in Liverpool between 2.00 and 3.00pm. "
1 CONT
1 CONT His family in Norway moved to the Segelstad farm and took the name of that farm but Hans had already emigrated to the USA and therefore kept the Myhre family name. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Death Certificate. Lived 20 years in Ramsey County, at 494 Ashland Ave. at time of death.  Was in Ancker Hospital (the city/county hospital that became St. Paul-Ramsey then Regions Hospital. Occupation, retired cashier.  Father Er
1 CONC ic, mother Emily?, born in Norway.  Cause of death, prostrate cancer. 
0 @N6000000001365390938@ NOTE Farmed the Segelstad farm until 1951 when sold. 
